---
description: Guidelines for using Mantine components in React components. Applies to *.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

Prefer using Mantine components (Grid, Box, Stack, Group, Container, etc.) and their native props over using the `style` prop or inline styles.

Be prescriptive about color and size on our visual components. Prefer a
short list of named options (`size: 'sm' | 'lg'`, `color: 'blue' | 'gray'`)
over `size: number`, hex strings, or one-off Mantine knobs (`px={4}`,
`size="compact-sm"`). Map tokens to pixels inside the component so call sites
stay in sync and engineers or AI have fewer choices. ImageResponse canvases
that must match a fixed PNG size are the exception.

```tsx
// Avoid — every caller picks a pixel size
size: number
<HomeIcon size={14} />

// Prefer — callers pick from a short list
size: 'sm' | 'lg'
<HomeIcon size="sm" />
```

When styling components:

- Use `Box` for wrapper elements that need spacing, padding, or other layout properties
- Use `Stack` for vertical layouts with spacing
- Use `Group` for horizontal layouts with spacing
- Use `Grid` for grid-based layouts
- Use `Container` for page-level containers with max-width constraints
- Prefer Mantine component props like `p`, `m`, `px`, `py`, `mt`, `mb`, `gap`, `spacing`, etc. over inline styles
- Use `sx` prop for more complex styling when needed, but prefer component props when possible

Examples:

```tsx
// ❌ Avoid
<div style={{ padding: 16, marginTop: 8 }}>
  <div style={{ display: 'flex', gap: 12 }}>
    {items}
  </div>
</div>

// ✅ Prefer
<Box p="md" mt="sm">
  <Group gap="md">
    {items}
  </Group>
</Box>
```

```tsx
// ❌ Avoid
<div style={{ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: 16 }}>
  {children}
</div>

// ✅ Prefer
<Stack gap="md">
  {children}
</Stack>
```

```tsx
// ❌ Avoid
<div style={{ maxWidth: 1200, margin: '0 auto', padding: '0 16px' }}>
  {content}
</div>

// ✅ Prefer
<Container size={1200} px="md">
  {content}
</Container>
```
